0..73 Comment "// A dependent arrow whose codomain ignores its binder is the plain arrow"
74..143 Comment "// . A family applied at its binder is a dependent codomain until the"
144..218 Comment "// family is read; a family that reads to one type at every argument makes"
219..290 Comment "// the function type over it the arrow to that type, in both directions"
291..357 Comment "// (Martin-Löf, _Intuitionistic Type Theory_, Bibliopolis, 1984)."
358..360 Comment "//"
361..390 Comment "// - see: #577 — `viaArrow`"
392..408 Comment "// The naturals."
